{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788705209494,"sessionID":"ses_f88de0697ffeJyEgaxJWCC7F93","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_cb5530a5dbbd42318708cab9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"include":"*.md","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-167","pattern":"module-as-function-routing|option C|routing-arm|@\\(route-groups"},"output":"Found 6 matches\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-167/plans/stdout-stderr-effect-model-research.md:\n  Line 5: \"a real type\" (option C, Effect/IO) and noting the program already has Stream-typed inputs and\n\n  Line 183: like it should be enough until `pipe_through` is the thing being built. Present option C as the\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-167/plans/module-routing-research.md:\n  Line 3: Research spike for the board row `module-as-function-routing-design` (gh:162). The question is\n\n  Line 129: **Candidate 3: `@path`, a dedicated routing-arm form (convention routing).**\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-167/plans/opencode-rollout.md:\n  Line 578: 2026-09-02 (option C, \"drop the poisoned issue-159 lane, re-board under a fresh lane id rather\n\n  Line 1011: time. Maintainer picked option C (drop and re-scope smaller), with a freeText addendum:\n","metadata":{"matches":6,"truncated":false},"title":"module-as-function-routing|option C|routing-arm|@\\(route-groups","time":{"start":1788705209478,"end":1788705209490}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me look at the board.yaml for the module-routing-syntax-build row, and the erlang-target-research.md, since the round was \"module-routing-and-erlang-target grilling round\". Maybe the round notes are in the erlang-target-research doc or somewhere.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_077237c83001UkQ2hC63bB6rPw","sessionID":"ses_f88de0697ffeJyEgaxJWCC7F93","messageID":"msg_077236eba001O82WfVppWVTyvq"}}
