{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788705210906,"sessionID":"ses_f88de0697ffeJyEgaxJWCC7F93","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_a26fbd29067e41be9b5c8bfa","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"module-routing-syntax-build|module-routing-and-erlang|module-as-function\" plans/board.yaml plans/board-archive.yaml"},"output":"plans/board.yaml:224:- id: module-routing-syntax-build\nplans/board.yaml:226:  title: 'Implement `@(path)` module-as-function routing-arm syntax -- ruled (module-routing-and-erlang-target round, question module-as-function-routing-design): option C (dedicated routing-arm form) chosen; maintainer refined the spelling from the round''s bare `@path` to parenthesized `@(route-groups/baz.toy)` because it encloses the path expression. See plans/module-routing-research.md.'\nplans/board.yaml:234:  title: 'Consider Erlang as an additional backend target, as a design stress test (maintainer note) -- round answer (module-routing-and-erlang-target round, question erlang-target-consideration): option C, spend more research and actually try the Erlang toolchain rather than accepting the desk-research-only finding (plans/erlang-target-research.md). Maintainer also flagged: concurrency will need to be supported by toylang regardless of this backend question -- worth surfacing as its own open item once this research lands.'\nplans/board-archive.yaml:1268:- id: module-as-function-routing-design\nplans/board-archive.yaml:1270:  title: 'Consider running other modules as functions, e.g. matcher arms dispatching to a submodule file (maintainer note) -- ruled (module-routing-and-erlang-target round, question module-as-function-routing-design): option C, `@path` dedicated routing-arm form, chosen over A ($(path) call-shaped) and B (path::fn named-function). Maintainer refined the spelling to parenthesized `@(route-groups/baz.toy)`. Spins off file-visibility-tracking-build (prerequisite, per the round''s own thesis that the checker doesn''t yet track per-file definition origin) and module-routing-syntax-build.'\nplans/board-archive.yaml:1277:  title: 'Checker tracks which file a definition came from and enforces per-call-site visibility -- prerequisite named by the module-as-function-routing-design ruling (module-routing-and-erlang-target round): the same gap that already blocks a `pub` prelude function from calling a private one blocks any module-dispatch syntax from meaning anything.'\n","metadata":{"output":"plans/board.yaml:224:- id: module-routing-syntax-build\nplans/board.yaml:226:  title: 'Implement `@(path)` module-as-function routing-arm syntax -- ruled (module-routing-and-erlang-target round, question module-as-function-routing-design): option C (dedicated routing-arm form) chosen; maintainer refined the spelling from the round''s bare `@path` to parenthesized `@(route-groups/baz.toy)` because it encloses the path expression. See plans/module-routing-research.md.'\nplans/board.yaml:234:  title: 'Consider Erlang as an additional backend target, as a design stress test (maintainer note) -- round answer (module-routing-and-erlang-target round, question erlang-target-consideration): option C, spend more research and actually try the Erlang toolchain rather than accepting the desk-research-only finding (plans/erlang-target-research.md). Maintainer also flagged: concurrency will need to be supported by toylang regardless of this backend question -- worth surfacing as its own open item once this research lands.'\nplans/board-archive.yaml:1268:- id: module-as-function-routing-design\nplans/board-archive.yaml:1270:  title: 'Consider running other modules as functions, e.g. matcher arms dispatching to a submodule file (maintainer note) -- ruled (module-routing-and-erlang-target round, question module-as-function-routing-design): option C, `@path` dedicated routing-arm form, chosen over A ($(path) call-shaped) and B (path::fn named-function). Maintainer refined the spelling to parenthesized `@(route-groups/baz.toy)`. Spins off file-visibility-tracking-build (prerequisite, per the round''s own thesis that the checker doesn''t yet track per-file definition origin) and module-routing-syntax-build.'\nplans/board-archive.yaml:1277:  title: 'Checker tracks which file a definition came from and enforces per-call-site visibility -- prerequisite named by the module-as-function-routing-design ruling (module-routing-and-erlang-target round): the same gap that already blocks a `pub` prelude function from calling a private one blocks any module-dispatch syntax from meaning anything.'\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"rg -n \"module-routing-syntax-build|module-routing-and-erlang|module-as-function\" plans/board.yaml plans/board-archive.yaml","time":{"start":1788705210902,"end":1788705210904}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The board.yaml is too large for grep. Let me look for the specific board row. Let me search for \"module-routing-syntax\" in board.yaml with rg and limit.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0772381f1001KHf7W8pZEwiPoW","sessionID":"ses_f88de0697ffeJyEgaxJWCC7F93","messageID":"msg_077237ca9001456msIkHexm0nu"}}
