{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788705221378,"sessionID":"ses_f88de0697ffeJyEgaxJWCC7F93","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_e6f112c897ed4d6db7e3e9a7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-167/justfile"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-167/justfile</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # List available recipes.\n2: default:\n3:     @just --list\n4: \n5: # The final gate: the full test suite. Landing requires this green.\n6: test:\n7:     cargo nextest run\n8: \n9: # The fast inner loop: skips the docs mega-test, the suite's ~137s long pole. Gate on `just test`.\n10: check:\n11:     cargo nextest run -E 'not test(every_fragment_is_a_real_program)'\n12: \n13: # Opt-in: run the skipped Euler 8/11/13/18 programs against real puzzle data in DIR, outside\n14: # `just test`. DIR holds your own copies of the raw data texts; fails loudly, never skips.\n15: euler-data DIR:\n16:     EULER_DATA={{DIR}} cargo nextest run --run-ignored ignored-only -E 'test(euler_real_data)'\n17: \n18: # Re-run the slow-fragment tier: the same suite, but `slow` fragments are executed on every\n19: # backend rather than only type-checked and emitted. The tier exists so `just test` stays fast;\n20: # this is where the deferred execution claim is re-verified.\n21: slow-test:\n22:     TOYLANG_SLOW=1 cargo nextest run\n23: \n24: # Run clippy with the repo's lint set, the same surface the Stop hook checks.\n25: clippy:\n26:     cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets\n27: \n28: # Time one benchmark (a name under benches/programs/) across every backend with hyperfine.\n29: # Design: plans/benchmark-plan.md. Results land in benches/results/<name>.{md,json}.\n30: bench NAME:\n31:     cargo run -q --bin bench -- {{NAME}}\n32: \n33: # Formatter check over every .toy file from the repo root down (exit 1 on drift).\n34: fmt:\n35:     cargo run -q --bin toylang -- fmt\n36: \n37: # Rewrite drifted files in place (same exit code as the check).\n38: fmt-write:\n39:     cargo run -q --bin toylang -- fmt --write\n40: \n41: # The repo's mechanical checks, the same surface the Stop hook runs.\n42: checks:\n43:     bash .claude/checks/run.sh\n44: \n45: # The autonomous drive loop: a tick every 600s, live colorized output, Ctrl-C to stop. Run ONE.\n46: drive:\n47:     .claude/scripts/drive-loop.sh\n48: \n49: # Fire one coordinator tick right now (zero tokens if there is nothing to do).\n50: tick:\n51:     .claude/scripts/drive-tick.sh\n52: \n53: # Watch the current coordinator tick live (detaches with Ctrl-C, tick untouched).\n54: peek:\n55:     .claude/scripts/tick-peek.sh\n\n(End of file - total 55 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# List available recipes.\ndefault:\n    @just --list\n\n# The final gate: the full test suite. Landing requires this green.\ntest:\n    cargo nextest run\n\n# The fast inner loop: skips the docs mega-test, the suite's ~137s long pole. Gate on `just test`.\ncheck:\n    cargo nextest run -E 'not test(every_fragment_is_a_real_program)'\n\n# Opt-in: run the skipped Euler 8/11/13/18 programs against real puzzle data in DIR, outside\n# `just test`. DIR holds your own copies of the raw data texts; fails loudly, never skips.\neuler-data DIR:\n    EULER_DATA={{DIR}} cargo nextest run --run-ignored ignored-only -E 'test(euler_real_data)'\n\n# Re-run the slow-fragment tier: the same suite, but `slow` fragments are executed on every\n# backend rather than only type-checked and emitted. The tier exists so `just test` stays fast;\n# this is where the deferred execution claim is re-verified.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-167/justfile","text":"# List available recipes.\ndefault:\n    @just --list\n\n# The final gate: the full test suite. Landing requires this green.\ntest:\n    cargo nextest run\n\n# The fast inner loop: skips the docs mega-test, the suite's ~137s long pole. Gate on `just test`.\ncheck:\n    cargo nextest run -E 'not test(every_fragment_is_a_real_program)'\n\n# Opt-in: run the skipped Euler 8/11/13/18 programs against real puzzle data in DIR, outside\n# `just test`. DIR holds your own copies of the raw data texts; fails loudly, never skips.\neuler-data DIR:\n    EULER_DATA={{DIR}} cargo nextest run --run-ignored ignored-only -E 'test(euler_real_data)'\n\n# Re-run the slow-fragment tier: the same suite, but `slow` fragments are executed on every\n# backend rather than only type-checked and emitted. The tier exists so `just test` stays fast;\n# this is where the deferred execution claim is re-verified.\nslow-test:\n    TOYLANG_SLOW=1 cargo nextest run\n\n# Run clippy with the repo's lint set, the same surface the Stop hook checks.\nclippy:\n    cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets\n\n# Time one benchmark (a name under benches/programs/) across every backend with hyperfine.\n# Design: plans/benchmark-plan.md. Results land in benches/results/<name>.{md,json}.\nbench NAME:\n    cargo run -q --bin bench -- {{NAME}}\n\n# Formatter check over every .toy file from the repo root down (exit 1 on drift).\nfmt:\n    cargo run -q --bin toylang -- fmt\n\n# Rewrite drifted files in place (same exit code as the check).\nfmt-write:\n    cargo run -q --bin toylang -- fmt --write\n\n# The repo's mechanical checks, the same surface the Stop hook runs.\nchecks:\n    bash .claude/checks/run.sh\n\n# The autonomous drive loop: a tick every 600s, live colorized output, Ctrl-C to stop. Run ONE.\ndrive:\n    .claude/scripts/drive-loop.sh\n\n# Fire one coordinator tick right now (zero tokens if there is nothing to do).\ntick:\n    .claude/scripts/drive-tick.sh\n\n# Watch the current coordinator tick live (detaches with Ctrl-C, tick untouched).\npeek:\n    .claude/scripts/tick-peek.sh","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":55,"totalLines":55,"truncated":false}},"title":"justfile","time":{"start":1788705221339,"end":1788705221374}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now let me understand the tests. Let me look at a corpus case and how `just check` works. Let me read the justfile and a sample corpus case.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_07723aad3001vKtRgo5xXPTZj7","sessionID":"ses_f88de0697ffeJyEgaxJWCC7F93","messageID":"msg_07723a426001I1Ma03uZw6lxhi"}}
