igration without asserting the stale expectation fence it cannot\n213:/// currently meet, and it means the gate cannot silently cover a broken fragment: compiling, or\n233:/// fails here, the same way a corpus case without fresh tags fails tag_corpus.\n294:/// Pulls the fragments out of one page. Malformed structure -- an `input` with no program, a\n295:/// program left without an expectation -- is a panic naming the line, like a malformed corpus\n296:/// case: a fence that asks for nothing looks exactly like a fence that passes.\n300:    fragments: &mut Vec<Fragment>,\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"rg -n \"case|corpus|fragment\" tests/docs.rs | head -40","time":{"start":1788705241747,"end":1788705241757}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Docs use `case` blocks that name corpus cases (`enum_match`, etc.). Let me check how tests/docs.rs handles those -- it likely maps `case` names to corpus cases. The docs harness \"every_fragment_is_a_real_program\" -- it compiles each fragment. Let me look at tests/docs.rs.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_07723fa75001MVESy8yW9P1THK","sessionID":"ses_f88de0697ffeJyEgaxJWCC7F93","messageID":"msg_07723f15f00100DYWmD80NLDWM"}}
